proxy_service: flush pending awards when the link returns during startup

ConnectivityMonitor.run probes once at its start and takes the answer as
its baseline. When the link came back between run_proxy_service's own
startup probe (offline, so no flush) and the monitor's first probe
(online), the monitor began from "online", saw no transition, and awards
earned offline stayed queued until the link next dropped and returned. At
the pin c7ebd1b6e7 upstream has no such handoff.

run_proxy_service hands its startup observation to the monitor
(initial_online); a first probe that is online after a startup that was
not flushes once, as a transition would have.

Written for ROCKNIX (fork issue pixelelated#588), added in f9b7ce3dfb. No
draft under docs/upstream/raofflineproxy/ yet (a #585 line, T19 PL-19).
Not sent (D-WORKFLOW-165).

--- a/linux/raofflineproxy/proxy_service.py
+++ b/linux/raofflineproxy/proxy_service.py
@@ -1089,6 +1089,7 @@
         self.interval_seconds = interval_seconds
         self.stop_event = threading.Event()
         self.watched_inodes = _capture_file_inodes([DATABASE_FILE])
+        self.initial_online = False
 
     def stop(self) -> None:
         self.stop_event.set()
@@ -1096,6 +1097,11 @@
     def run(self) -> None:
         was_online = self.server.refresh_reachability(force_probe=True)
         save_online_state(was_online)
+        # Carry the startup observation across the first worker probe. A link
+        # returning between them must not become an unhandled online baseline.
+        if was_online and not self.initial_online and not self.stop_event.is_set():
+            LOGGER.info("Connectivity restored; attempting flush")
+            self.server.flush_pending_awards()
         while not self.stop_event.wait(self.interval_seconds):
             if self.watched_inodes and _files_replaced_underneath(self.watched_inodes):
                 # A reinstall deleted our log/database out from under this
@@ -1469,6 +1475,7 @@
         if initial_online:
             server.flush_pending_awards()
             retry_storage_corruption_report(config_data)
+        connectivity_monitor.initial_online = initial_online
         connectivity_monitor.start()
         periodic_refresh.start()
         cache_queue_worker.start()
